-# VS Code Agents Instructions
+# LOCALCODERS — AUTONOMOUS AGENT TEAM DIRECTIVES
 
-This file provides instructions for AI coding agents working with the VS Code codebase.
+This document specifies mandatory engineering and design protocols for all agents working on LocalCoders.
 
-For detailed project overview, architecture, coding guidelines, and validation steps, see the [Copilot Instructions](.github/copilot-instructions.md).
+---
+
+## MANDATORY UI/UX DIRECTIVE: UI/UX PRO MAX INTELLIGENCE
+
+Whenever ANY agent (Main Agent, Frontend Specialist, UI/UX Designer, Component Specialist, Code Review / Critic Agent, or subagent) performs ANY user interface, component, styling, layout, interaction, or webview task, it **MUST STRICTLY FOLLOW THE UI/UX PRO MAX DESIGN SYSTEM INTELLIGENCE**.
+
+The universal design skill is permanently installed at:
+- `.agents/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md`
+- Master Design System: `design-system/localcoders/MASTER.md`
+- Search Script: `python3 .agents/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py`
+
+### Mandatory 6-Step UI/UX Workflow
+
+For every frontend or UI/UX task, agents MUST execute these steps:
+
+1. **Read & Follow the Skill**:
+   Inspect `.agents/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md` and `design-system/localcoders/MASTER.md` before making any layout or styling changes.
+
+2. **Search for Targeted Design System Recommendations**:
+   Execute the local search script for component/pattern guidance:
+   ```bash
+   python3 .agents/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py "<component or interaction pattern>" --design-system
+   ```
+   Or query specific domains (e.g. `--domain ux`, `--domain icons`, `--domain typography`).
+
+3. **Select Verified Visual Styles, Colors, Typography & Spacing**:
+   - **Theme**: Dark Mode (OLED / Deep Slate) Developer Tool aesthetic.
+   - **Backgrounds**: Deep black/slate (`#0F172A`, `#0B0F19`).
+   - **Cards & Surfaces**: Dark slate surfaces (`#1E293B`, `#161F30`).
+   - **Borders & Separators**: Subtle, low-contrast borders (`rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)` / `#334155`).
+   - **Accents**: Sky Blue (`#38BDF8`), Run Green (`#22C55E`), Indigo glow (`#818CF8`).
+   - **Typography**: Primary code font `JetBrains Mono` / UI font `IBM Plex Sans`, `-apple-system`, `Inter`.
+   - **Spacing Tokens**: Systematic 4px/8px grid (`--space-xs: 4px`, `--space-sm: 8px`, `--space-md: 16px`, `--space-lg: 24px`).
+
+4. **Enforce Accessibility & Interaction Guidelines**:
+   - **NEVER use raw emojis as icons**. Always use professional inline SVG icons (Lucide/Codicons/Heroicons) with proper `aria-hidden="true"` or accessible labels.
+   - Ensure `cursor: pointer` is set on every clickable element.
+   - Smooth hover & active transitions (150ms–200ms ease).
+   - High contrast text (`#F8FAFC` on dark surfaces, minimum 4.5:1 ratio).
+   - Visible keyboard focus rings (`:focus-visible` with `outline: 2px solid #38bdf8`).
+   - Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
+
+5. **Apply Recommendations to Real Implementation**:
+   Implement actual, working CSS/HTML/TypeScript within the VS Code desktop workbench, webviews, and auxiliary panels. Ensure all controls are backed by real runtime services, IPC handlers, and state management.
+
+6. **Review Visual & Functional Quality**:
+   Audit the modified interface against the UI/UX Pro Max pre-delivery checklist:
+   - [x] No raw emojis as UI icons (use clean SVGs)
+   - [x] Pointer cursor on interactive controls
+   - [x] Smooth 150-250ms transitions
+   - [x] WCAG AAA / AA contrast
+   - [x] Keyboard navigable and visible focus rings
+   - [x] Responsive flex/grid layouts with collapsible sidebars
+
+---
+
+## AGENT ROLES & DESIGN RESPONSIBILITIES
+
+### 1. Main Agent (Lead Architect)
+- Oversees overall desktop IDE ergonomics and ensures strict separation between **Agent View** (3-column Devin cockpit) and **IDE View** (classic Monaco workbench with docked AI assistant).
+- Guarantees **exactly one authoritative chat composer** is visible at all times.
+- References `design-system/localcoders/MASTER.md` for all global layout decisions.
+
+### 2. Frontend Specialist / UI/UX Agent
+- Directly queries `.agents/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py` before authoring any webview HTML, CSS, or client JavaScript.
+- Enforces professional Dark Mode tokens, typography scale, icon consistency, and layout responsiveness.
+
+### 3. Component Specialist
+- Crafts reusable, accessible UI elements (buttons, popovers, segmented bars, chips, drawers, status badges) adhering to UI/UX Pro Max specifications.
+- Replaces raw emoji decorators with precision vector SVGs.
+
+### 4. Code Review / Critic Agent
+- Audits all UI pull requests and changesets against UI/UX Pro Max quality standards, accessibility rules, and theme consistency.
+- Rejects any code introducing emoji icons in place of SVGs, missing focus states, or unstyled controls.
diff --git a/bin/localcoders b/bin/localcoders
new file mode 100755
index 00000000..1c518cd3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bin/localcoders
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -e
+
+cleanup() {
+  # Mandate: When user closes the IDE, stop all background processes and unload Ollama models to release GPU VRAM & memory
+  if command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    running_models=$(curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/ps 2>/dev/null | grep -o '"name":"[^"]*"' | cut -d'"' -f4 || true)
+    for model in $running_models; do
+      curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate -d "{\"model\": \"$model\", \"keep_alive\": 0}" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
+    done
+  fi
+  # Clean up any child worker processes
+  pkill -P $$ 2>/dev/null || true
+}
+
+trap cleanup EXIT INT TERM
+
+SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "$(readlink -f "$0")")" && pwd)"
+ROOT_DIR="$(dirname "$SCRIPT_DIR")"
+VSCODE_SKIP_PRELAUNCH=1 "$ROOT_DIR/scripts/code.sh" "$@"
